   "subject": "Re: limit of shiny.maxRequestSize() when deploying application on web with RStudio Server Pro",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">RStudio Server Pro is for developing Shiny applications, not deploying them. Shiny Server Pro is used for deploying. There is no max file or memory limit imposed by Shiny itself, but there are obviously going to be inherent limits due to the machine and operating system that you should test yourself first.<div><br></div><div>Hope that helps!</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
